From 08de5c93a135d7cc32bb475a6ceffdfdf0d85ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:29:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat(chexc): re-parent the 26 obvious unchecked exception
 classes (proposal 6.4)

Applies the non-UNCERTAIN half of notes/stdlib-exception-inventory.md: every class the
classification principle decides unambiguously (contract / state / index / arithmetic /
unwrap -> unchecked) now derives from std.core.UncheckedException, so throwing one no
longer demands a capability and listing one in a 'throws' clause is rejected.

Roots only -- subclasses (OverflowException, FSException-style chains) inherit the status.
PrettyException keeps its PrettyPrintable conjunct. The 23 UNCERTAIN classes are untouched
and keep producing warnings under warn-mode checking, pending author rulings.

Verified: std builds clean; CheckedExceptions suite + API/std/{core,unittest/mock,
overflow,collection} 400/400 (one SIGSEGV in test_tree_map_coverage under the parallel
run passes in isolation -- load flake, same class as the earlier MacroTest
oversubscription); a minimal runtime probe confirms catch-at-subclass, catch-at-Exception
and direct throw/catch all behave through the new hierarchy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
